{"content":[{"c":["ZAREPHATH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Village where the woman who provided food and lodging for Elijah lived (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.17.9-10","r":"1Kgs.17.9-10","rawR":"1Kgs.17.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.17.9-10","value":"1Kgs.17.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 17:9-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.4.26","r":"Luke.4.26","rawR":"Luke.4.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.4.26","value":"Luke.4.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 4:26"},"). Obadiah later prophesied that the Israelite exiles of Halah would “possess Phoenicia as far as Zarephath” (",{"href":"?bref=Obad.1.20","r":"Obad.1.20","rawR":"Obad.1.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Obad.1.20","value":"Obad.1.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ob 1:20"},"). Zarephath was under the control of Sidon at the time Elijah visited, thus serving as a safe haven from King Ahab of Israel. Zarephath is likely identifiable with modern Surafend, where a chapel marks the traditional site for the widow’s house."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Zarephath","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 17:9-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.17.9-10","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.17.9-10","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.17.9-10"},{"anchorText":"Lk 4:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.4.26","rawQueryValue":"Luke.4.26","sourceRefExact":"Luke.4.26"},{"anchorText":"Ob 1:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Obad.1.20","rawQueryValue":"Obad.1.20","sourceRefExact":"Obad.1.20"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"712fa765db9276bbd80a90aa7217f72b92b41cb49b22c6a73ac41517ad3a3bea","sourceItemName":"Zarephath","sourceItemOrder":35,"sourceMember":"Articles/Z.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Zarephath","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Zarephath","title":"Zarephath","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}